<body>

<section class="hero">

<img src="captain-two-toes.png" alt="Captain Two Toes">

<h1>Captain Two Toes</h1>

<h2>Half the Toes. All the Legend.</h2>

</section>

<section class="story">

<div class="quote">
"Ahoy! I'm Captain Two Toes. Folks always ask how I lost eight toes... but only me oldest mate, McKaster, knows the truth."
</div>

<p>
No one remembers my real name anymore.
From the Gulf Coast to the Atlantic, sailors simply know me as <strong>Captain Two Toes.</strong>
</p>

<p>
Ask me how I lost eight toes and you'll hear a different tale every time. Sometimes it was a shark. Sometimes a sea serpent. Once I claimed I traded them to an old sea witch for "the best sea legs ever known."
</p>

<p>
Only my oldest friend, <strong>McKaster</strong>, knows the truth—and he's never told a soul.
</p>

<p>
All anyone knows is that I came home from one mysterious voyage with only my two big toes remaining... and somehow became the surest-footed sailor on the ocean.
</p>

<p>
My pirate flag bears two footprints instead of crossed swords, and my crew has long suspected I have an unusual appreciation for feet.
</p>

<p>
I can recognize a sailor by their footprints in the sand, insist on yearly Foot Readiness Inspections, and have been known to admire a fine pair of boots... perhaps a little too much.
</p>

<p>
No one is quite sure if it's admiration... or something more.
No one is brave enough to ask.
</p>

<p>
After all, I've never abandoned a sailor, never broken my word, and never lost a battle at sea.
</p>

<div class="quote">
If you ever find yourself aboard my ship and I compliment your arches...
<br><br>
<strong>You might want to keep your shoes on.</strong>
</div>

</section>

<footer>
☠️ Captain Two Toes • Half the Toes. All the Legend. ☠️
</footer>

